-- title:
--   PM ✱1: formulas, the theorems of ✱1, truth tables
-- statement:
--   **DRAFT** — part of an in-progress public formalization of *Principia Mathematica*; it may still change, and every change is dated in the project's [change log](https://github.com/willmcginnis/principia-mathematica-lean/blob/main/docs/EXPORT_LOG.md).
--
--   The primitive apparatus of Whitehead and Russell's *Principia Mathematica*, ✱1 (Vol. I, 1910, pp. 98–101), as a deep embedding.
--
--   1. **Formulas** $\mathcal F$: propositional variables, negation ${\sim}p$ and disjunction $p \lor q$, PM's two primitive ideas.
--   2. **Defined connectives**, as PM's definitions: $p \supset q := {\sim}p \lor q$ (✱1·01), $p \land q := {\sim}({\sim}p \lor {\sim}q)$ (✱3·01; PM writes $p\,.\,q$), $p \equiv q := (p \supset q) \land (q \supset p)$ (✱4·01).
--   3. **Theorems of ✱1**: the least set of formulas containing the primitive propositions
--
--   $$
--   \begin{aligned}&(p \lor p) \supset p &&(✱1·2,\ \text{Taut})\\ &q \supset (p \lor q) &&(✱1·3,\ \text{Add})\\ &(p \lor q) \supset (q \lor p) &&(✱1·4,\ \text{Perm})\\ &(p \lor (q \lor r)) \supset (q \lor (p \lor r)) &&(✱1·5,\ \text{Assoc})\\ &(q \supset r) \supset ((p \lor q) \supset (p \lor r)) &&(✱1·6,\ \text{Sum})\end{aligned}
--   $$
--
--   for all formulas $p, q, r$, and closed under the rule ✱1·1: from $p$ and $p \supset q$ infer $q$.
--   4. **Truth tables**: the two-valued value of a formula under a valuation, the variables of a formula, and the decidable test that a formula is a tautology.
--
--   The card of each numbered proposition of ✱1–✱5 states that its formula is a theorem of ✱1 in this sense.
--
--   **Formalization Note** PM states the primitive propositions with real variables and a rule of substitution; here they are schemas over arbitrary formulas, which has the same effect (✱1·11).
--
--   Source: [PM.Basic](https://github.com/willmcginnis/principia-mathematica-lean/blob/2e43991fec4221198853c15ba637b6c8430cec4b/PM/Basic.lean).
-- source:
--   Whitehead and Russell, Principia Mathematica, Vol. I (1910), ✱1–✱5; formalization: https://github.com/willmcginnis/principia-mathematica-lean/blob/2e43991fec4221198853c15ba637b6c8430cec4b/PM/Basic.lean

